<title>ITALY: POLL-Italy seen issuing 12.25 trln lire BOTs.</title>
<headline>POLL-Italy seen issuing 12.25 trln lire BOTs.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian Treasury is expected on average to issue 12.25 trillion lire worth of short-term bills (BOTs) at auction on July 10 against 13.5 trillion lire worth of paper maturing, analysts polled by Reuters said.</p>
<p>The Treasury is also expected to offer 1.5 trillion lire of 18-month zero coupon certificates (CTZs) and 2.0 trillion lire of 24-month CTZs.</p>
<p>The Treasury will detail the amounts on offer at the mid-month auction on Monday, July 7.</p>
<p>Following are the analysts' forecasts (in trillion lire):</p>
<p>		 3-Mo    6-Mo     12-Mo    Total     18-Mo    24-Mo</p>
<p>		 BOT     BOT	 BOT	BOT	 CTZ	CTZ</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Bank America 3.75     4.25     4.50    12.50     1.50     2.00</p>
<p>Caboto	 4.00     4.00     4.00    12.00     1.50     2.00</p>
<p>BCI	    4.00     4.25     4.50    12.75     1.50     2.50</p>
<p>Credito	3.50     4.50     4.50    12.50     1.50     2.00</p>
<p>DeutscheBank 3.50     4.00     4.00    11.50     1.50     2.00</p>
<p>================================================================</p>
<p>CONSENSUS    3.75     4.25     4.25    12.25     1.50     2.00</p>
<p>Maturing     3.50     5.00     5.00    13.50	--	 --</p>
<p>================================================================</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 6129589</p>
</text>
